  "id": "scapular-retraction",
  "name": "Scapular Retraction",
  "definition": "A strict open-chain scapular isolation whose concentric phase retracts one scapula against anterior elastic resistance while the shoulder is held near 80 degrees of flexion and the elbow remains extended. The initial contract admits only McCabe et al.'s directly prescribed unilateral Theraband fixture: middle trapezius is primary by action specificity, lower trapezius is secondary, and the measured upper-trapezius and serratus activity is treated as scapular co-contraction rather than evidence that either produces retraction. The source measured EMG rather than three-dimensional scapular kinematics, so rows, reverse flies, pull-aparts, face pulls, prone raises, cable variants, and every fixture with dynamic glenohumeral or elbow motion remain outside this narrow contract.",
  "evidenceRefs": [
    "mccabe-2007-below-90-scapular-exercises",
    "cools-2004-isokinetic-scapular-rotators"
  ],
